 filePrep:'Step 1: Match the required dimensions. Use CMYK artwork at 300 dpi with 1/16 inch bleeds on all sides, unless your product template specifies otherwise.\nStep 2: Embed all images and outline your text.\nStep 3: Export a print-ready PDF with bleeds. Check both sides, page order and orientation before uploading.',
 fileGuide:'',
 wallGuide:'Measure the widest and tallest points of your wall in inches. Add the extra trimming allowance recommended for your project. Prepare a clean, dry, smooth wall and let fresh paint cure fully. Lay out panels in order; align the first panel carefully and smooth from the centre outward. Trim edges only after checking the alignment. Follow the supplied material-specific instructions.\nFlat Matte gives a smooth, low-reflection finish. Texture adds a tactile surface and visual depth. Removable and permanent adhesives have the same price; choose for your wall and intended duration. Test adhesion first—removable does not guarantee damage-free removal on every painted surface.',
 detailingIntro:'A cleaner cabin. A deeper shine. A finish worth protecting. Choose a starting plan and we will tailor it to your vehicle.',
 detailingAftercare:'Before your visit, remove personal belongings and tell us about stains, pet hair, paint damage or previous coatings. We inspect the vehicle and confirm your plan before starting. After detailing, use gentle pH-balanced wash products and clean microfibre towels. Follow the curing and first-wash guidance supplied for your coating.',
